(Clearly, we have a fundamental misalignment in the customer experience—our growth stagnation points to a) Tj
T* (structural issue much deeper than just features or onboarding. You need to ask, "What is the real game being) Tj
T* (played here?" Our customers are not just looking for more features or an easier onboarding route; they’re) Tj
T* (seeking transformation and partnership in their journey.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (When I spoke with Lenny, we discussed displacing where value lies. Right now, our customers have not only) Tj
T* (unmet needs but also a lack of true engagement and collaboration from us. They aren't leaving because they) Tj
T* (can't access features or onboarding; they are potentially feeling unsupported in their larger goals. ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (So, instead of investing in a time-consuming overhaul of either features or onboarding, let’s think structurally. I) Tj
T* (bet that building a customer success program that marries immediate onboarding improvements with deeper) Tj
T* (strategic collaborations—like architectural assessments—will renew their trust and spark retention. Prioritize the) Tj
T* (engineering bandwidth to create that collaborative framework. Time to own our role in shifting the narrative from) Tj
T* (merely service providers to invaluable partners. ) Tj
T* () Tj
